{"qid":"Q408","names":["Commonwealth of Australia"],"title":"Commonwealth of Australia","endonym":{"native":"Australia","lang":"en-au"},"capsule":"The Commonwealth of Australia was inaugurated on 1 January 1901, federating the six self-governing British colonies of New South Wales, Victoria, Queensland, South Australia, Western Australia, and Tasmania under a written constitution with a Westminster-style parliament. The federation acquired the Northern Territory from South Australia and established the Australian Capital Territory in 1911 for the purpose of a new national capital, Canberra, which opened in 1927; Australian administration of Papua, transferred from Britain under the 1905 Papua Act, had already begun in 1906. Australia gained effective independence through the Statute of Westminster Adoption Act (1942, backdated to 1939) and the Australia Acts (1986), and today exercises sovereignty over a continental landmass plus island territories, as our dataset records to 2024.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Australian federal and state boundaries are precisely surveyed; the dataset geometry from 1905 onward accurately reflects constitutional borders; external territories and Antarctica claims are well-documented but administratively distinct from the mainland federation.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Britannica: Australia - Indigenous, Colonization, Federation","url":"https://www.britannica.com/place/Australia/History"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Australia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australia"}],"britannica":"place/Australia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Australia","rulers":[{"qid":null,